.TH MARBOR\-NODE 1 "2026-08-17" "marbor dev" "Marbor Manual"
.SH NAME
marbor\-node \- node control driver operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marbor node
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
node control driver operations
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B control
show or accept a node's control driver
.TP
.B control probe <node>
show a node's control\-driver status (configured + discovered)
.TP
.B control accept <node>
accept a control driver + identifier for a node
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-driver string
control driver: systemd, docker, process, launchd, or windows_service (required)
.TP
.B \-\-identifier string
driver\-specific identifier (unit name, container name, PID file path, plist label, service name) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-start-command string
launch command for the process driver's Start action (only meaningful when \-\-driver=process)
.RE
.TP
.B control clear <node>
clear the accepted control driver for a node
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
confirm without prompting
.RE
.TP
.B agent
manage marbor agent lifecycle for a node
.TP
.B agent get <node>
show a node's marbor agent config (does not display the auth token)
.TP
.B agent enable <node>
enable or reconfigure the marbor agent for a node
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-port int
agent port (required) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-scheme string
http or https (empty = keep existing, or http on first enable)
.RE
.TP
.B agent disable <node>
disable the marbor agent for a node
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
confirm without prompting
.RE
.TP
.B agent regenerate <node>
issue a fresh token for an already\-enabled marbor agent
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmarbor\fR(1)
